{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grdbpersistence"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"GRDBPersistence"}],"externalID":"GRDBPersistence","title":"GRDBPersistence","role":"collection"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DatabaseStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"RecordStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","type":"reference"},{"text":") for apps on Apple platforms that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already keep a GRDB database. It takes the app’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseQueue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabasePool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a table","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"name, creates the table with a migration of its own, and opens no second SQLite database. It is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"product of its own, which ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves out.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It makes the same promises as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The tracker’s worker commits each record, in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"transaction of its own, before publishing it. A batch’s rows are marked before any destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives it and deleted once every destination has. The table holds at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"byteBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bytes of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoded records, 5 MiB by default, with the oldest rows deleted to make room, and each drop is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported on ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseStore.dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Records are encoded as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" encodes them, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same events are kept: every ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the program and the library’s own, or only the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseStore(events:database:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists. Rows written by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Traffluent 0.0.44 or earlier, in an earlier encoding, aren’t read: each is deleted when the store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"opens and reported as ","type":"text"},{"code":".undecodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or as ","type":"text"},{"code":".versionMismatch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where its stored version differs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from its type’s.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"How durable a commit is against power loss is the database’s choice, through its journal mode and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"synchronous","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" setting. ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseStore.synchronize()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" checkpoints a database in WAL mode; call it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the app moves to the background. Open one store per table at a time, and don’t open one from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inside an access to the same database.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app with no database of its own uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":", which needs no GRDB."}]},{"code":["import GRDB","import GRDBPersistence","","let database = try DatabaseQueue(path: databasePath)","let store = try DatabaseStore(database: database, table: \"analyticsRecord\")","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what a store keeps, its bounds and recovery.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"API","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"API"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where this module’s API isn’t there, so its symbols","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have no pages of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for an Apple target.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Keeping-records-in-a-database","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Keeping records in a database"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DatabaseStore","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStoreError"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"GRDBPersistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence","title":"Persistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","role":"collection"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/persistingrecords":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Persisting Records","type":"text"}],"title":"Persisting Records","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords"}}}